Title: F1-M04 — Hold the Switchyard (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

INT. RAIL SIGNAL BOX - DUSK

[[AMBIENCE: wind through broken glass, a signal lever clanking, far-off locomotive]]
[[MUSIC: restrained military tension]]

A track diagram is chalked on the signal box wall. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(serious)
The switchyard feeds every forward position on this front. If it falls, reinforcements will arrive one at a time.

MIRA
(measured)
The enemy has enough armour to test every approach. Engineers need eighteen minutes to disable the rail spur.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: switchyard at centre with signal box, north road and choke point, canal with a damaged bridge to the south, rail spur running east, observation tower on the north road]]

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(firm)
Build layered defences and hold the yard until the rail line is cut. Do not let the engineers be overrun.

MIRA
(dry)
Eighteen minutes is the crew's estimate, not mine. If they are interrupted once, the clock does not restart; it just keeps running.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(pointing at map)
Towers where the north road narrows. Rockets behind them. The repair truck stays out of the line.

MIRA
(analytical)
The canal bridge to the south is down. Nothing in this sector is equipped to fix it, so on paper the north road is their only lane.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(neutral)
On paper. Watch the south anyway.

MIRA
(concerned)
One more thing from the convoy fight. Every time we settled into a pattern, they changed theirs. I want to see if that holds here.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
